  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "The original post I have found is this one: https://vrchat.canny.io/feature-requests/p/allow-world-owners-to-set-private-worlds-available-to-friends but I would like to bring the conversation up again since seemingly nothing has happened.\nLately I've seen alot of \"memory\" worlds where its a cute (or basic) home world with pictures all over the walls, and I've even considered doing it for myself. But I think a good idea would be for the world creator to be able to upload it so that only friends are able to see it/save it etc. Like what the original post said with the \"friends open\" suggestion, but I do think having all three of those suggestions would work really good as well.\nIt also might help creators that want to test out a world with multiple people (especially now with the grow in games that use udon) before pushing it to be public and having people be in/use a potentially broken and unfinished world.",
